      },
      "id": 9900,
      "options": {
        "content": "<div style=\"font:13px/1.6 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#c7ccd1;border-left:3px solid #B77D34;padding:8px 0 8px 14px\"><b style=\"color:#e7ebee\">Thermal &amp; Power area.</b> Three boards, no overlap. Everything is read from <code>node-exporter</code> hwmon and DCGM on the 1,898 GB300 trays.<div style=\"margin-top:8px;display:flex;gap:26px;flex-wrap:wrap\"><span><a href=\"/d/nvis-bmc-thermal\" style=\"color:#7FB3E8;text-decoration:none\">&#9656; Tray Sensors &amp; Module Meters</a><br><span style=\"color:#8b9298\">live hwmon temperatures against each sensor's vendor critical limit, and the six ACPI module power meters per tray</span></span><span><a href=\"/d/nvis-bms-facility\" style=\"color:#7FB3E8;text-decoration:none\">&#9656; Thermal History &amp; Energy</a><br><span style=\"color:#8b9298\">peak-since-boot sensor high-water marks, zone-resolved ACPI thermal zones, and energy integrated from the DCGM counter</span></span></div><div style=\"margin-top:8px;color:#8b9298\">GPU core/HBM temperature, GPU power draw and the DCGM violation counters are owned by <a href=\"/d/gpu-health\" style=\"color:#7FB3E8;text-decoration:none\">GPU Health</a> and <a href=\"/d/gpu-errors\" style=\"color:#7FB3E8;text-decoration:none\">GPU Error Surface</a> and are deliberately not repeated here.</div></div>",
        "mode": "html"
      },
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
